-- Foster's sum (1949): the charges' parts of a unit pair across each line add to n − 1, so where every line is
-- alike (the hexagon, the cage, the diamond net closed on itself with n vertices and 2n lines) a pair one line
-- apart has (n − 1)/m of a line's energy: 5/6, 3/4, and (n − 1)/(2n) on the net, 1/2 less 1/(2n)
fs-foster : (if eqb (fs-foster-sum 6 ring6 ring6) (times 5 (spanning-trees 6 ring6)) then (if eqb (fs-foster-sum 10 cage10 cage10) (times 9 (spanning-trees 10 cage10)) then eqb (fs-foster-sum 4 complete4 complete4) (times 3 (spanning-trees 4 complete4)) else false) else false) ≡ true
fs-foster = λ i → true
